            <ArticleTitle>Thigh neuralgia as a symptom of obturator hernia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>457-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A material of 8 patients with obturator hernias is presented. In 7 of the patients a neuralgic pain in the thigh was the main symptom and a hyperesthesia in the cutaneous segment of the obturator nerve was also common. A recognition and an early operation of this condition is important, since the mortality is high when an intestinal obstruction has complicated the disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
